Add QtTesting include directories to qMRMLWidgets for system (non-superbuild) builds.

CTKQtTesting does not re-export the QtTesting include directory, but Slicer's
qMRML*EventPlayer / qMRML*EventTranslator headers include <pqWidgetEventPlayer.h>
and other pq* headers directly. In Slicer's own superbuild the QtTesting build
tree is added to the include path explicitly (External_CTK.cmake); a system
QtTesting build has no such wiring, so AUTOMOC of qMRMLWidgets fails with
"pqWidgetEventPlayer.h: No such file or directory". Resolve the QtTesting
imported target and add its include dirs.

--- a/Libs/MRML/Widgets/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-02 15:46:36.204091766 -0700
+++ b/Libs/MRML/Widgets/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-02 15:46:36.216875345 -0700
@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@
   list(APPEND CTK_LIBRARIES
     CTKQtTesting
     )
+  # In a non-superbuild (system QtTesting) build, CTKQtTesting does not
+  # re-export the QtTesting include directory, yet Slicer's qMRML*EventPlayer
+  # and qMRML*EventTranslator headers include <pqWidgetEventPlayer.h> and
+  # other pq* headers directly. Resolve the QtTesting imported target and add
+  # its include dirs so the sources and AUTOMOC-generated moc files compile.
+  find_package(QtTesting REQUIRED)
+  include_directories(${QtTesting_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 endif()
 
 # --------------------------------------------------------------------------
